{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["FB5", "FB6", "U8", "U11"],
      "pins": ["U8.12", "U8.17", "U11.12", "U11.17", "FB5.1", "FB5.2", "FB6.1", "FB6.2"],
      "nets": ["/NET0024", "/NET0086", "/NET0085", "/NET0044"],
      "observed": "FB5 connects U8 VDD_ISO (pin 17, net /NET0024) to U8 V_ISO (pin 12, net /NET0086). FB6 connects U11 VDD_ISO (pin 17, net /NET0085) to U11 V_ISO (pin 12, net /NET0044). The VSEL pins are set by resistor dividers (R52/R38, R22/R5) to about 1.23 V, which is likely a logic low, selecting V_ISO = 5 V. Thus the 5 V isolated rail is shorted to the 3.3 V isolated rail through the ferrite beads.",
      "expected": "The isolated 5 V (V_ISO) and 3.3 V (VDD_ISO) rails should be separate, or VSEL should be tied to VDD_ISO to make V_ISO = 3.3 V. The specification states each isolated EZO channel derives its own isolated +5 V supply.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"28\") (name \"/NET0024\") ... (node (ref \"FB5\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"17\") (pinfunction \"VDD_{ISO}\") (pintype \"power_out\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"86\") (name \"/NET0086\") ... (node (ref \"FB5\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"12\") (pinfunction \"V_{ISO}\") (pintype \"power_out\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Each isolated EZO channel (U3 for pH, U4 for EC) derives its own isolated +5V (/V_pH, /V_EC) and isolated ground (/GNDISO_pH, /GNDISO_EC) internally from the ADM3260's isoPower feature"}
      ],
      "impact": "Short between 5 V and 3.3 V isolated rails, causing excessive current, possible damage to ADM3260 or ferrite beads, and incorrect supply to EZO modules.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["C12"],
      "pins": ["C12.1", "C12.2"],
      "nets": ["NET0042", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "C12 pin 1 is on net NET0042 (ESP32 IO1/ADC1, J3 pin 2), and pin 2 is on +3V3. It is a 100 nF capacitor between a GPIO and the 3.3 V supply.",
      "expected": "A decoupling/filter capacitor on a GPIO should connect to GND, as C6 does for IO0 (C6 pin 1 on GND, pin 2 on NET0029).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"79\") (name \"NET0042\") ... (node (ref \"C12\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"C12\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The capacitor does not filter noise to ground; it couples the GPIO to the 3.3 V rail, potentially causing noise or affecting the GPIO signal.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["D2", "T5", "R8"],
      "pins": ["D2.1", "D2.2", "T5.1", "R8.1", "R8.2"],
      "nets": ["/NET0021", "GND", "/+24V_F"],
      "observed": "D2 is a 12 V zener with cathode (pin 1) on /NET0021 (T5 gate) and anode (pin 2) on GND. R8 is between T5 gate and source (/+24V_F).",
      "expected": "For P-channel reverse-polarity protection, the zener should be between gate and source (cathode to source, anode to gate) to clamp Vgs and turn off the MOSFET during reverse polarity. Connecting it to GND allows the zener to forward-conduct during reverse polarity, turning the MOSFET on.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"25\") (name \"/NET0021\") ... (node (ref \"D2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"K\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (node (ref \"T5\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\") (pintype \"passive\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"72\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"D2\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "Reverse polarity protection fails; the P-channel MOSFET may turn on during reverse polarity, allowing reverse current and potentially damaging the board.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies: the isolated 5 V and 3.3 V rails are bridged via FB5/FB6, C12 is incorrectly connected to +3V3 instead of GND, and the reverse-polarity protection zener D2 is connected to GND instead of the MOSFET source."
}

